task('keyword-intent-map','Keyword intent mapping','SEO','Assign each search intent to one useful page and a clear next action.',[
'Collect actual customer questions and search terms before expanding the keyword list. Keep a distinction between service buyers and people researching a problem.',
'Group terms by the action the visitor needs next, then choose one existing URL to own each intent. Similar phrases usually belong on the same page.',
'Check the proposed page against existing service pages and articles. Add a new URL only when its answer and useful deliverable are different.',
'Review query-to-page performance after enough settled data exists; change the mapping when the page receiving impressions is not the intended owner.'],[
('Service buyer','{query} for {segment}','Dedicated {service} scope and a path to speak with the {buyer}.'),('Assessment question','{service} assessment for {segment}','Explain {intent}; avoid inventing a price or arrival commitment.'),('Scope question','{objection}','Use the existing service page if it already answers this question completely.'),('Not a fit','{exclude}','Review context before adding an exclusion or deciding that the inquiry is irrelevant.')],
'Query-to-page alignment and qualified inquiries by intent group.','Publishing a separate page for every synonym can split signals and create overlapping answers.',SEARCH)
task('service-page-outline','Service landing page outline','SEO','Design a page that answers a qualified buyer’s scope and next-step questions.',[
'Lead with the service and property context, not a string of locations or an unsupported ranking claim.',
'Explain what is assessed, what evidence is available, and where the offered service stops. Put the next action near the first useful explanation.',
'Use project evidence only with permission. A clear process or scope document is better than an invented testimonial.',
'Check the page on a phone, follow every important link, and confirm that a real person or booking flow receives the inquiry.'],[
('Opening promise','{service} for {segment}','Explain help for {need}; identify the next assessment or conversation.'),('Decision context','Who coordinates the work?','Write for the {buyer}, with attention to {priority}.'),('Evidence block','{proof}','Add {segment_proof}; use only verified business details.'),('Action block','Start a scope conversation','Request {fields}; explain what happens after contact.')],
'Qualified contact actions from the page and the share that reach an appropriate next stage.','A visually impressive page still fails if the scope is unclear or the contact action is broken.',SEARCH)
task('content-brief','Content brief template','Content','Give a writer a bounded, evidence-based brief instead of a keyword count.',[
'Name the buyer’s question and the decision the content should help them make. List material that must be gathered before drafting.',
'Choose a format that fits the question: comparison, checklist, explanation, or worked example. Set a clear boundary around what the article does not establish.',
'Collect original evidence and have the service team check accuracy. Label hypothetical examples rather than presenting them as completed projects.',
'Link the article to a relevant service page and related explanation without making every paragraph a sales pitch.'],[
('Audience','{buyer}','Account for {constraint}'),('Primary question','{objection}','Answer directly before expanding into background.'),('Required evidence','{asset}','Support the service explanation with {proof}.'),('Useful next action','Prepare a service conversation','Use {fields}; link to the relevant {service} service page.')],
'Engaged visits that proceed to a relevant resource or qualified contact action.','A brief that specifies word count but no buyer question encourages generic content.',SEARCH)
task('faq-answer-plan','FAQ answer planning','Content','Answer the objections that prevent a service buyer from taking the next step.',[
'Gather questions from calls, scope conversations, and sales notes. Remove personal incident details before using those notes in content.',
'Write the shortest complete answer first, then explain the conditions that change the answer. Do not imply an outcome that the service team cannot verify.',
'Keep the answer visible on the page. Do not add structured data for content visitors cannot access or assume FAQ markup produces a search feature.',
'Review questions after the team changes its service scope, scheduling process, or documentation requirements.'],[
('Core question','{objection}','Explain the next decision for the {buyer}.'),('Scope question','What does {service} include for {segment}?','State the actual service boundary: {boundary}'),('Intake question','What should I prepare before contacting you?','Ask for {fields}; avoid unnecessary sensitive information.'),('Coordination question','Who handles project communication?','Use this handoff: {handoff}')],
'Fewer avoidable clarification loops and more qualified next-step requests.','A universal answer about price, coverage, or completion can mislead buyers when the scope varies.',SEARCH)
task('internal-linking-plan','Internal linking plan','SEO','Help visitors move between the service answer, supporting evidence, and next action.',[
'Start with a real page inventory. Record each destination’s purpose and keep one preferred URL for each intent.',
'Add links where the reader needs context. The anchor should describe the destination, not repeat an exact phrase across every page.',
'Use a small set of relevant supporting pages. A large block of unrelated keyword links makes navigation harder.',
'Crawl the new links after deployment. Confirm that the destination exists, resolves as intended, and uses the correct canonical URL.'],[
('Service destination','{service} overview','Anchor: {service} service scope for {segment}.'),('Supporting evidence','{asset}','Place the link beside the claim or process it actually supports.'),('Related question','{objection}','Connect to a distinct answer, not another version of the same page.'),('Contact action','Speak with the team','Explain the next action for the {buyer} and the requested {fields}.')],
'Reachable useful destinations, zero orphan pages, and resolved internal links.','Sitewide blocks of near-identical exact-match links do not replace contextual navigation.',SEARCH)
task('technical-seo-audit','Technical SEO audit checklist','SEO','Verify that a useful page can be crawled, rendered, and understood at its intended URL.',[
'Check the final response and canonical URL on the deployed host. A page that canonicals to a different site is not ready to represent this URL in search.',
'Confirm that robots rules, page directives, authentication, and navigation allow the intended access. Look at the actual rendered page, not just the build result.',
'Validate titles, headings, important text, and links without relying on client-side scripts for the main answer.',
'Use a sitemap for discovery, then inspect actual crawl and indexing evidence separately. A sitemap submission is not an indexing guarantee.'],[
('URL owner','{service} for {segment}','Use one self-referencing canonical for the final page.'),('Main answer','{intent}','Make the service scope and the next action available in rendered HTML.'),('Primary path','Contact the {buyer}','Check desktop and phone navigation and the final destination.'),('Evidence log','Deployment and inspection dates','Record status, canonical, indexability, and verified errors rather than assuming success.')],
'Correct response, indexable directives, valid canonical, and crawl evidence when available.','A successful deployment does not prove that Google crawled or indexed the page.',CANON)
task('service-area-page-plan','Service-area content planning','SEO','Explain real operating coverage without inventing offices or mass-producing city substitutions.',[
'Use the company’s actual service boundaries and operating capacity. Confirm where an office exists and where the company only travels to customers.',
'Explain what changes for the buyer in the area: access, project coordination, service fit, and available local evidence.',
'Combine closely overlapping location pages when they provide the same answer. Do not create location-specific claims without local evidence.',
'Keep local profile details consistent with the real business, and review coverage when dispatch or staffing changes.'],[
('Service coverage','{service} for {segment}','Verify operating coverage before naming a place in copy.'),('Buyer context','{buyer}','Address {priority}; do not imply a local branch from a service area alone.'),('Local evidence','Approved project or process detail','Use {proof} only where it genuinely applies.'),('Eligibility check','Real location and service area','Follow official profile rules; no virtual-office shortcuts.')],
'Accurate coverage information and qualified inquiries from areas the company actually serves.','Changing city names without adding a different useful answer can create overlapping pages.',GBP)
task('ai-search-readiness','AI search readiness checklist','SEO','Make the page helpful and technically eligible without relying on invented AI-specific requirements.',[
'Answer the buyer’s question in plain language and keep the important explanation accessible as text.',
'Support claims with original evidence and relevant sources. Explain limitations and the difference between an example and a verified result.',
'Apply normal search fundamentals: crawl access, sensible internal links, appropriate canonicals, and a good page experience.',
'Track available referrals and search performance without assuming every AI mention is measurable or that a special file guarantees inclusion.'],[
('Direct answer','{objection}','Start with the practical next decision for the {buyer}.'),('Evidence','{asset}','Use {proof}; keep examples and confirmed outcomes distinct.'),('Service boundary','{boundary}','Remove unsupported guarantees and unrelated claims.'),('Technical eligibility','Visible text and crawl access','Follow Google’s normal search guidance; no special AI markup is required.')],
'Accessible useful answers and measurable referral or search activity where data is available.','Treating an AI text file or special schema as a guaranteed inclusion mechanism distracts from page quality.',AI)
task('gbp-services-checklist','Google Business Profile service checklist','Local search','Keep a profile’s services aligned with the actual business and the landing page.',[
'Confirm the profile represents a real eligible business and an authorized location. A service-area page does not create eligibility for another profile.',
'List only services the team actually provides. Explain the scope consistently across the profile, website, and intake process.',
'Check the destination page and contact details. A user should not encounter a different service or an unconfigured form after clicking.',
'Review profile changes through an authorized account and keep a dated record of the business facts used.'],[
('Service name','{service}','Use the business’s real offered service, not an unrelated query variant.'),('Website destination','Scope for {segment}','Explain {intent} to the {buyer}.'),('Evidence check','{proof}','Avoid unsupported qualifications or invented locations.'),('Contact consistency','{fields}','Use a reachable destination and a clear next action.')],
'Accurate services, consistent business details, and qualified profile-originated inquiries.','Extra profiles for unstaffed or invented offices can create eligibility and accuracy problems.',GBP)
task('project-photo-plan','Project photo and proof plan','Local search','Collect useful service evidence with permission and without exposing private information.',[
'Define what each image or document should explain before collecting it. A generic gallery is less useful than evidence tied to a buyer question.',
'Obtain permission and remove identifying or sensitive details that are not needed to understand the project.',
'Write captions that describe the actual work and context. Do not let a photo imply an outcome, qualification, or service that was not provided.',
'Store an approval record and review image performance and page speed when publishing.'],[
('Project context','{service} for {segment}','Show an approved view that supports {intent}.'),('Buyer reassurance','{segment_proof}','Explain what the image establishes and what it does not.'),('Supporting artifact','{asset}','Use a redacted or anonymized version where necessary.'),('Approval record','Permission and caption review','Avoid publishing customer identities, incident details, or valuables by default.')],
'Approved evidence used in the right service context with clear captions and suitable file sizes.','Stock images or sensitive project photos should not be presented as verified customer proof.',SEARCH)
task('review-request-workflow','Review request workflow','Local search','Ask for honest feedback consistently after a real customer interaction.',[
'Choose a genuine service milestone and confirm the appropriate contact. Do not select recipients based on whether they are likely to leave a favorable review.',
'Keep the request neutral and optional. Do not offer incentives, request a specific rating, or ask the customer to include scripted keywords.',
'Provide a direct feedback path and respect communication preferences. Remove sensitive project details from the message.',
'Record that the request was sent without storing unnecessary customer information in the marketing worksheet.'],[
('Recipient','Authorized {buyer}','Use the contact who actually experienced the service.'),('Context','Completed {service} interaction','Do not request feedback for work that did not occur.'),('Request draft','Thank you for working with our team','Invite honest feedback about the experience; keep it optional.'),('Privacy check','{segment}','Avoid property details or personal incident descriptions in the request.')],
'Consistent neutral requests and useful customer feedback, not a target rating.','Filtering unhappy customers out of public review requests can distort feedback.', 'https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114')
task('multi-location-reporting','Multi-location reporting plan','Local search','Compare real locations without confusing office coverage, lead ownership, and service areas.',[
'Create a location inventory from verified business facts. Separate physical locations, eligible profiles, and areas served.',
'Use a stable location ID in marketing and CRM reports. Give shared campaigns and cross-area inquiries an explicit attribution rule.',
'Compare locations using the same definitions for qualified inquiries, opportunities, and outcomes.',
'Review anomalies with the operating team before moving spend or rewriting a location’s service coverage.'],[
('Location record','Verified location ID','A page serving {segment} does not establish an additional office.'),('Service record','{service}','Confirm which real teams can accept the requested work.'),('Lead ownership','{buyer} inquiry','Record both originating source and assigned operating location.'),('Outcome definition','Qualified next step','Use the same stage criteria across locations; log transfers separately.')],
'Consistent location-level inquiry and opportunity reporting with transparent transfer rules.','Counting transferred inquiries twice can make location performance look better than it is.',GBP)
task('paid-search-ad-groups','Paid search ad-group mapping','Paid search','Align a buyer’s search, an honest ad, and a relevant service page.',[
'Group search terms by the actual service and the next decision. Keep research queries distinct from direct provider searches.',
'Use current account search-term evidence to refine groups. Treat suggested keywords as candidates until real relevance is observed.',
'Match ad language and landing-page scope. A campaign should not offer work the company cannot perform or accept.',
'Review qualified outcomes by group rather than optimizing only for inexpensive clicks.'],[
('Provider intent','{query} for {segment}','Landing answer: {intent}.'),('Buyer context','{buyer}','Address {priority} in the destination page.'),('Ad-to-page consistency','{service}','Do not promise a result or arrival window absent operating confirmation.'),('Review queue','{exclude}','Inspect actual term context before exclusion.')],
'Qualified opportunities by ad group and transparent spend-to-outcome reporting.','Combining every damage-related term in one group makes it harder to understand relevance.',ADS)
task('negative-keyword-worksheet','Negative keyword worksheet','Paid search','Identify irrelevant demand without excluding valuable inquiries by accident.',[
'Start with actual search terms and classify the reason each term is or is not relevant.',
'Consider employment, training, supplies, and unrelated consumer intent separately. A word can be useful in one query and irrelevant in another.',
'Choose the negative match type deliberately. Negative keywords behave differently from positive keywords and do not automatically cover every close variant.',
'Log the reason, match type, and review date. Revisit exclusions if qualified inquiries disappear from an otherwise relevant segment.'],[
('Candidate exclusion','{exclude}','Example only; confirm against account search terms before adding.'),('Audience mismatch','{negative}','Review the full query rather than excluding a broad industry word.'),('Protected intent','{query} for {segment}','Avoid excluding service terms that the {buyer} legitimately uses.'),('Change log','Term, match type, reason, reviewer','Record the intended effect and check results after the change.')],
'Reduced irrelevant traffic with retained qualified service demand.','A broad negative based on one bad query can suppress legitimate searches.',NEG)
task('search-ad-copy','Search ad copy brief','Paid search','Write relevant service advertising using verified capabilities and a clear next action.',[
'Choose one service intent and buyer context for the draft. Make the service understandable without needing a clever slogan.',
'Use only verified business facts. Do not invent response times, certifications, guarantees, prices, or local offices to improve the headline.',
'Pair each proposed message with the page section that substantiates it.',
'Check current platform policy and asset limits in the account before publishing, then evaluate qualified outcomes rather than click rate alone.'],[
('Headline concept','{service_short} for {segment}','Editorial concept; edit for the current platform’s character limits.'),('Description concept','Discuss {intent}','Describe the assessment and next action without promising an outcome.'),('Evidence concept','{asset}','Link the claim to approved supporting material.'),('CTA concept','Speak with our team','Write for the {buyer}; explain what is needed to begin.')],
'Ad relevance, qualified landing actions, and downstream opportunities.','High click-through rate does not justify a misleading promise or a mismatch with the destination.',ADS)
task('paid-landing-page-audit','Paid landing page audit','Paid search','Check the entire path from a search ad to a usable service conversation.',[
'Compare the actual query and ad promise with the first screen of the destination.',
'Check that the buyer can identify service fit, evidence, limitations, and the next action without hunting through unrelated navigation.',
'Test on a phone and follow the action through the booking or contact destination. Avoid sending test leads without authorization.',
'Connect source and outcome records so the team can distinguish clicks, submissions, qualified inquiries, and accepted opportunities.'],[
('Message match','{service} for {segment}','Opening answer should address {intent}.'),('Buyer friction','{constraint}','Keep the action appropriate to the {buyer}.'),('Trust check','{proof}','Use only evidence that supports the exact offer.'),('Routing check','{handoff}','Confirm the person receiving the inquiry can move it forward.')],
'Usable qualified-contact completion and the opportunity rate after the page.','A form-success screen is not evidence that the business received a useful inquiry.',ADS)
task('campaign-budget-scenario','Campaign budget scenario','Paid search','Use explicit assumptions to estimate a planning range without presenting market forecasts as facts.',[
'Collect the company’s own spend, inquiry, qualification, and outcome records. Keep missing values blank until they can be supported.',
'Write each conversion stage as a separate assumption. Do not mix a lead conversion rate with a sale rate or compare incompatible reporting periods.',
'Calculate scenarios and change one input at a time. Label all example values as hypothetical.',
'Use operating capacity and observed qualified outcomes to decide whether a test should expand, contract, or pause.'],[
('Scope','{service} for {segment}','Keep this scenario separate from other services or buyer segments.'),('Inputs','Spend, CPC, contact rate, qualification rate','Use observed account data or explicitly labeled assumptions.'),('Output formula','Spend ÷ CPC × contact rate × qualification rate','This estimates qualified inquiries only; it does not establish jobs or revenue.'),('Decision check','{buyer}','Review whether the operating team can accept the projected inquiry mix.')],
'Actual qualified inquiry cost compared with the stated planning assumptions.','Illustrative conversion rates are not industry benchmarks or guaranteed results.',ADS)
task('geographic-targeting-plan','Geographic targeting plan','Paid search','Match campaign geography to the work the company can actually accept.',[
'Begin with verified service coverage and operating constraints, not a list of attractive place names.',
'Review the current platform’s location settings and reports. Separate a person’s location, a location mentioned in a query, and the property needing service.',
'Use CRM property-location data to inspect the quality of inquiries and log out-of-area requests.',
'Change coverage only after checking capacity and the effect on qualified outcomes.'],[
('Service capability','{service}','Do not imply an office in every targeted area.'),('Property context','{segment}','Ask for {fields} to identify the actual service location.'),('Routing requirement','{handoff}','Match coverage with the team that can accept the project.'),('Exclusion review','Outside real operating coverage','Document the reason and inspect actual inquiry locations.')],
'Qualified inquiries within verified service coverage and accepted project mix.','Targeting a broad region does not establish that every lead or property is inside the service area.',ADS)
task('call-action-qa','Call action QA checklist','Conversion','Make phone actions accurate, usable, and connected to the intended business process.',[
'Confirm the displayed number, link destination, hours claims, and routing rules against verified operating information.',
'Test the phone link’s format and accessibility on a mobile device without placing an unsolicited call.',
'Check any tracking-number behavior for consistency across page content and the call destination.',
'Use authorized test procedures for call routing, then compare call records with qualified inquiries rather than treating every call as a lead.'],[
('Page context','{service} for {segment}','The call action must explain the service being discussed.'),('Buyer preparation','{fields}','Keep the initial information appropriate to the {buyer}.'),('Promise check','{boundary}','A call button must not introduce an unsupported availability claim.'),('Handoff check','{handoff}','Verify the correct destination through the team’s authorized QA process.')],
'Correct call destinations, answered relevant calls, and accurate qualification records.','A prominent tap-to-call button is ineffective when it reaches the wrong number or an unprepared team.',SEARCH)
task('call-intake-script','Call intake script','Conversion','Help the first conversation establish service fit and a clear authorized next step.',[
'Begin with the broad service request and location, then identify the caller’s relationship to the property.',
'Ask only what is necessary to route the inquiry. Do not turn marketing intake into diagnosis, technical inspection, or sensitive-data collection.',
'Restate the requested next action and identify who is responsible for following up.',
'Record the source, qualification result, and handoff in the CRM so later reporting reflects the actual conversation.'],[
('Opening','What help are you looking for with {service}?','Use plain language; do not assume the cause or scope.'),('Authority','Who coordinates this {segment} property?','Identify the {buyer} or another authorized contact.'),('Service-specific questions','{qualify}','Keep safety, health, and technical decisions with qualified professionals.'),('Close and route','{handoff}','Confirm the next action and the responsible person.')],
'Complete relevant intake records and fewer avoidable transfers or repeated questions.','A long script can increase friction and collect information that is not needed to qualify the inquiry.',SEARCH)
task('quote-request-form','Quote request form specification','Conversion','Collect enough information for a useful reply without implying an instant binding scope or price.',[
'Define who will review the request and what they need to decide the next step.',
'Keep required fields limited to routing and contact essentials. Label optional fields clearly and explain why any additional detail helps.',
'Provide accessible labels, validation, and failure states. A submit button should not silently discard information or claim receipt when the destination is unavailable.',
'Confirm consent and data handling with the business’s actual process before enabling the form.'],[
('Required fields','{fields}','Tailor to the {buyer}; avoid personal health, resident, or incident information.'),('Scope description','Request a {service} conversation','Do not present the form as a completed inspection or guaranteed quote.'),('Service boundary','{boundary}','Explain any assessment needed before a scope can be discussed.'),('Routing outcome','{handoff}','State the next step and the receiving team accurately.')],
'Successfully received, relevant requests with enough information to act.','More fields do not automatically produce better leads and may discourage legitimate buyers.',SEARCH)
task('mobile-cta-test','Mobile CTA test plan','Conversion','Check whether a phone visitor can understand the offer and take the intended action.',[
'Test the first screen at representative phone widths and with larger text. Verify that the service and primary next action remain visible and readable.',
'Open the menu, follow the main action, and inspect the destination. A sticky control must not obscure content, consent, or form buttons.',
'Check keyboard focus, accessible labels, and whether hidden controls are removed from interaction.',
'Use one defined primary action per test and compare qualified completion rather than only button clicks.'],[
('First-screen question','Is this {service} for {segment}?','Show the buyer’s next decision: {intent}.'),('Primary action','Start a service conversation','Make the path clear for the {buyer}.'),('Friction check','{constraint}','Avoid overlays or wide controls that block the task.'),('Completion check','{fields}','Confirm the final destination supports the required information.')],
'Qualified mobile completions with no overflow or obstructed controls.','A visible CTA click can still end in a broken calendar, inaccessible form, or wrong contact destination.',SEARCH)
task('booking-flow-audit','Booking flow audit','Conversion','Make the transition from a page to a scheduled conversation clear and honest.',[
'Confirm that the booking calendar belongs to the intended business and appointment type.',
'Explain what the appointment is for, who should book, and what information helps the team prepare.',
'Check the destination in a separate session without booking an appointment unless testing is authorized.',
'Ensure the business can distinguish a booking from an attended, qualified conversation in reporting.'],[
('Appointment purpose','Discuss {service} for {segment}','Set expectations around {intent}, not an on-site inspection unless that is what is offered.'),('Attendee','{buyer}','Ask whether another decision maker should join.'),('Preparation','{fields}','Keep preparation proportionate and avoid sensitive attachments.'),('Next-stage record','Booked → attended → qualified','Do not count all bookings as accepted projects.')],
'Working booking destinations and attended qualified conversations.','A calendar link for the wrong appointment type creates a misleading conversion path.',SEARCH)
task('lead-routing-workflow','Lead routing workflow','Conversion','Send a relevant inquiry to the team that can act while preserving source and ownership.',[
'Define routing by actual service fit, operating coverage, buyer authority, and current capacity.',
'Choose a clear owner for unmatched or incomplete requests. Do not let missing optional fields silently discard a legitimate inquiry.',
'Keep source attribution attached when transferring the record, and prevent multiple teams from creating duplicate opportunities.',
'Test expected failure and transfer cases through an authorized process, then review unassigned records.'],[
('Service route','{service}','Confirm the business actually accepts this scope.'),('Buyer route','{buyer} for {segment}','Use {fields} to identify the responsible party.'),('Operational handoff','{handoff}','Record the receiving owner and next action.'),('Exception route','Incomplete or mismatched request','Keep a review queue; document why the inquiry is or is not a fit.')],
'Assigned qualified inquiries, successful transfers, and low duplicate-record rates.','Automation that hides unmatched requests can make the dashboard look cleaner while losing real opportunities.',SEARCH)
task('missed-call-follow-up','Missed-call follow-up plan','Conversion','Provide an appropriate next contact after an unanswered service inquiry.',[
'Check whether the business has permission and an appropriate basis to follow up through the intended channel.',
'Use a short message that identifies the business and invites the caller to state the broad service need.',
'Avoid including sensitive property or incident details in an automated message. Respect opt-outs and channel preferences.',
'Record whether contact was made, whether the inquiry fits, and who owns the next action.'],[
('Context','Missed inquiry about {service}','Do not assume the project details from a number alone.'),('Recipient','Potential {buyer}','Confirm identity and authority before sharing project information.'),('Draft','We missed your call. How can our team help?','Keep the message neutral and identify the business.'),('Follow-up record','Contacted, qualified, assigned','Use {handoff} once the service need is understood.')],
'Recovered relevant conversations and accurate follow-up records.','Automated messages can expose information or annoy recipients when identity and permission are assumed.',SEARCH)
task('referral-partner-plan','Referral partner outreach plan','Partnerships','Build a relevant professional introduction around a real service need and clear boundaries.',[
'Choose partners whose work genuinely intersects with the requested service and property type.',
'Explain the company’s actual scope, communication process, and handoff requirements without promising payments or outcomes.',
'Offer a useful service overview or coordination checklist rather than a vague request for leads.',
'Record permission and the agreed next step. Review any commercial referral arrangement with the business before proposing terms.'],[
('Service intersection','{service} for {segment}','Explain the need: {need}.'),('Professional audience','Contacts who support the {buyer}','Use a relevant introduction rather than a scraped bulk contact list.'),('Useful artifact','{asset}','Show how project communication and service boundaries work.'),('Handoff agreement','{handoff}','Specify what a useful introduction contains and how it is handled.')],
'Relevant partner conversations and properly attributed qualified introductions.','A referral plan should not invent incentive terms or send generic mass messages.',SEARCH)
task('facilities-outreach-brief','Facilities buyer outreach brief','Partnerships','Frame a concise, relevant service introduction for an authorized property contact.',[
'Understand the recipient’s role and the type of property decision they can make.',
'Lead with a service coordination problem the recipient can recognize, not an exaggerated disaster scenario.',
'Offer a practical scope or communication overview and make the next step optional.',
'Use an appropriate contact channel and keep outreach respectful, limited, and relevant.'],[
('Role','{buyer}','Confirm the person’s responsibility for {segment}.'),('Opening angle','{priority}','Connect the introduction to a real coordination task.'),('Proof offered','{segment_proof}','Use {proof}; avoid unsupported client claims.'),('Next step','A short service-fit conversation','Prepare {fields} if the recipient wants to continue.')],
'Relevant replies and agreed next steps with the right decision maker.','A contact’s job title does not establish that the person controls every part of the property’s scope.',SEARCH)
task('inquiry-email-follow-up','Inquiry email follow-up template','Sales operations','Help an interested contact move from an inquiry to a clear service conversation.',[
'Reference the recipient’s stated inquiry without repeating sensitive details unnecessarily.',
'Ask one clear next-step question and identify any information required for routing.',
'Use a specific business signature and a reliable contact destination. Do not send attachments with private customer examples.',
'Record the reply or closure reason and avoid treating silence as consent to a long sequence.'],[
('Subject concept','Your {service} inquiry','Keep the subject clear and non-alarming.'),('Opening','Thank you for contacting our team','Acknowledge the request for {segment} without inventing project facts.'),('Question','Who should coordinate the next conversation?','Ask for the {buyer} and appropriate {fields}.'),('Close','Confirm the next action','Use {handoff}; give a simple way to reply or decline.')],
'Useful replies and completed next actions from genuine inquiries.','An aggressive sequence can create more messages without creating a better customer experience.',SEARCH)
task('case-study-brief','Case study interview brief','Content','Gather permissioned evidence that explains the work without inventing results.',[
'Obtain approval to discuss the project, including what details, images, names, and outcomes may be published.',
'Describe the starting situation, the agreed scope, the work process, and the documented outcome separately.',
'Attribute numerical results to actual records and define the time period and measurement method.',
'Give the customer and service team a review opportunity before publication, especially where context could identify people or operations.'],[
('Project context','{service} for {segment}','Explain the original request and who authorized the work.'),('Evidence to gather','{asset}','Include {proof}; anonymize where needed.'),('Process question','How did you coordinate {priority}?','Use the actual project record rather than a generic success claim.'),('Outcome boundary','What can be documented?','Do not infer revenue, coverage, health, or reopening outcomes from an image.')],
'Approved case studies with traceable evidence and clearly defined outcomes.','A polished story should not turn hypothetical metrics into customer results.',SEARCH)
task('strategy-call-agenda','Strategy call agenda','Sales operations','Use a first marketing conversation to clarify scope, buyer fit, and evidence needs.',[
'Start with the business goal and the services the company actually wants to grow.',
'Map the inquiry path from search through contact, qualification, and accepted opportunity.',
'Ask for existing evidence and operating constraints before discussing a forecast or campaign expansion.',
'End with a named owner, the information required, and an agreed next step rather than an unsupported promise.'],[
('Service focus','{service} for {segment}','Identify why this segment matters to the business.'),('Buyer journey','{buyer}','Discuss {priority} and who approves the next step.'),('Current evidence','Search terms, inquiries, and outcomes','Use actual records; keep unmeasured assumptions explicit.'),('Next action','A documented service-fit plan','Gather {asset} and confirm the appropriate handoff.')],
'Clear scope, missing-data list, owner, and agreed next action.','A strategy call is not enough evidence to promise a ranking, lead volume, or return.',SEARCH)
task('thirty-day-launch-plan','30-day campaign launch plan','Sales operations','Sequence evidence, implementation, QA, and measurement before scaling activity.',[
'Use the first stage to confirm service scope, real coverage, buyer fit, and available proof.',
'Prepare the page, messaging, routing, and measurement together so the campaign has a working destination.',
'Run authorized QA of the visitor path and inspect failure states before opening a larger test.',
'Use the final stage to review actual inquiry quality and decide what to change next; the schedule is a planning sequence, not a results guarantee.'],[
('Stage 1','Confirm {service} and {segment} fit','Identify the {buyer}, service boundaries, and {asset}.'),('Stage 2','Build the customer path','Explain {intent}; collect only the necessary {fields}.'),('Stage 3','Verify delivery and routing','Apply {handoff}; inspect mobile and contact failure cases.'),('Stage 4','Review qualified outcomes','Compare observed results with the stated assumptions and capacity.')],
'Completed launch prerequisites and a documented first outcome review.','Scaling spend or publishing more pages before the contact path works increases waste.',SEARCH)
task('utm-naming-plan','UTM naming plan','Measurement','Keep campaign links readable and consistent without putting private information into URLs.',[
'Define a small controlled vocabulary for source, medium, campaign, and optional content labels.',
'Keep labels about the campaign, not the individual visitor. Never place customer names, email addresses, property details, or incident descriptions in tracking parameters.',
'Test the destination and analytics reporting, and preserve attribution when the inquiry moves into the CRM.',
'Document naming changes so reporting does not split the same campaign into several inconsistent labels.'],[
('Source / medium','example-partner / referral','Illustrative labels; replace with the actual referring channel.'),('Campaign','{service_slug}-{segment_slug}','Use a stable campaign label for {service} and {segment}.'),('Content','service-overview','Describe the creative or placement, not the customer.'),('CRM mapping','Source → inquiry → opportunity','Keep the {buyer} relationship in the CRM, not in public query parameters.')],
'Consistent campaign attribution with no private information in tracking URLs.','A long unique UTM string is not better if it leaks personal details or breaks naming consistency.',GA)
task('lead-qualification-scorecard','Lead qualification scorecard','Measurement','Define service fit transparently before comparing channels or rejecting inquiries.',[
'Choose criteria the business actually uses: service match, coverage, authority, scope stage, and ability to accept the work.',
'Use simple documented states instead of an unexplained total score. Keep incomplete information separate from a confirmed mismatch.',
'Apply the same definitions across channels so one source is not judged more harshly than another.',
'Review rejected and unassigned records for errors. Never score people using sensitive personal characteristics or inferred health information.'],[
('Service fit','Requested {service}','Confirm the scope rather than inferring it from the keyword.'),('Property fit','{segment}','Check operating capability and access requirements.'),('Authority / coordination','{buyer}','Use {fields} to identify who can take the next step.'),('Disposition','Qualified / needs review / out of scope','Document the reason and use {handoff} when appropriate.')],
'Consistent qualification decisions with a reason recorded for every disposition.','An arbitrary numerical score can hide why a legitimate inquiry was dismissed.',SEARCH)
task('pipeline-report-template','Pipeline report template','Measurement','Show the stages between a marketing contact and an accepted business opportunity.',[
'Define the reporting period and the meaning of each stage before collecting totals.',
'Keep inquiries, qualified inquiries, appointments, accepted opportunities, and completed outcomes distinct.',
'Deduplicate transferred or repeat contacts and show unknown source separately rather than forcing attribution.',
'Reconcile marketing totals with the operating system and review exceptions with the team that handles the work.'],[
('Segment','{service} for {segment}','Keep the service and property context attached to every stage.'),('Inquiry','A genuine contact record','A click or page view is not an inquiry.'),('Qualified opportunity','Documented service fit and next step','Confirm the {buyer} and {handoff}.'),('Outcome / attribution','Recorded stage and known source','Show unknown and transferred records explicitly; avoid double counting.')],
'Consistent stage counts and traceable movement from source to accepted opportunity.','Reporting every call as a lead and every booking as revenue overstates performance.',GA)
task('qualified-lead-cost-calculator','Qualified lead cost calculator','Measurement','Calculate a clear unit cost using real spend and consistently qualified inquiries.',[
'Use the same period and service segment for spend and inquiry records.',
'Choose whether the calculation includes media only or a broader set of marketing costs and label that choice.',
'Deduplicate inquiries and apply a documented qualification definition.',
'Divide eligible cost by the qualified inquiry count; show an undefined result when the denominator is zero rather than a misleading zero-cost figure.'],[
('Scope','{service} for {segment}','Do not mix unrelated services into the denominator.'),('Numerator','Eligible marketing cost','State media-only or all-in cost and the reporting period.'),('Denominator','Deduplicated qualified inquiries','Confirm service fit and the {buyer} relationship.'),('Formula','Eligible cost ÷ qualified inquiries','This is not cost per job unless the denominator is actually accepted jobs.')],
'Qualified inquiry cost with an explicit cost scope and qualification definition.','Comparing media-only CPL with an all-in acquisition cost mixes different measures.',GA)
task('marketing-roi-worksheet','Marketing contribution worksheet','Measurement','Separate revenue, marketing cost, and project contribution in an explicit scenario.',[
'Define which outcomes and costs belong to the campaign and time period.',
'Use recorded outcome values and actual project costs where available. Keep estimates labeled and do not assume all revenue is profit.',
'Show the difference between return on ad spend and contribution after costs.',
'Use scenarios to examine assumptions, then reconcile with actual records before making a spending decision.'],[
('Campaign scope','{service} for {segment}','Keep the audience and reporting period consistent.'),('Revenue measure','Attributed accepted or completed revenue','State which one is used and how attribution was assigned.'),('Cost measure','Marketing cost plus relevant project costs','Avoid treating the full project value as contribution.'),('Contribution formula','Revenue − project costs − marketing costs','A worked scenario is not a promise of future profit.')],
'Documented attributed outcomes and cost assumptions that reconcile to business records.','ROAS and profit are different calculations; neither proves causation by itself.',GA)
task('seasonal-content-calendar','Seasonal content calendar','Content','Plan useful publishing around observed customer questions and actual operating capacity.',[
'Use the business’s own inquiry history and approved service calendar before asserting a seasonal pattern.',
'Choose topics that help customers make a real decision at the relevant stage.',
'Prepare evidence and review dates in advance so content does not become a collection of unsupported weather or demand claims.',
'Compare published topics with actual query and inquiry evidence and update the plan when conditions differ.'],[
('Planning theme','{service} for {segment}','Use observed demand; do not assume a seasonal spike.'),('Buyer question','{objection}','Answer the question in the context of the {buyer}.'),('Evidence needed','{asset}','Collect {proof} before scheduling publication.'),('Operational check','Capacity and handoff','Confirm {handoff} and current service availability before promoting the page.')],
'Useful timely content supported by real inquiry evidence and operating capacity.','A calendar date does not justify inventing local weather, demand, or competition statistics.',SEARCH)
task('service-comparison-brief','Service comparison brief','Content','Explain meaningful choices and service boundaries without disparaging unnamed competitors.',[
'Identify the buyer’s real alternatives and the decision criteria that change the choice.',
'Describe each option using verifiable scope differences, not invented competitor weaknesses.',
'Show what information the buyer should gather before deciding and where the company’s service does or does not fit.',
'Link to the relevant service details and update the comparison when scope changes.'],[
('Decision','Which {service} scope fits {segment}?','Start with {intent}.'),('Buyer criteria','{priority}','Explain why the {buyer} may evaluate these factors.'),('Boundary','{boundary}','Do not imply every provider offers the same services.'),('Evidence requested','{proof}','Use {segment_proof} to make the comparison concrete.')],
'Clearer service-fit decisions and fewer mismatched inquiries.','A comparison filled with unverified competitor claims does not help the buyer assess the work.',SEARCH)
task('review-response-guide','Review response guide','Content','Respond professionally to feedback without exposing project details or escalating a dispute.',[
'Read the feedback and confirm what can be discussed publicly under the business’s privacy and communication process.',
'Acknowledge the feedback without confirming sensitive customer or incident details.',
'Offer an appropriate private contact path when a response requires account-specific context.',
'Escalate substantive complaints to the responsible business team and record the follow-up without arguing publicly.'],[
('Service context','{service}','Do not disclose the scope of an individual customer’s project.'),('Property context','{segment}','Keep occupants, operations, belongings, and incident details private.'),('Neutral response','Thank you for sharing your feedback','Use a respectful reply; do not request a revised rating as a condition of help.'),('Private resolution','Authorized business contact','Route to the team responsible for the {buyer} relationship.')],
'Professional replies and documented resolution steps with privacy preserved.','A detailed public rebuttal can reveal customer information even when the business believes it is correct.','https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114')
task('buyer-guide-outline','Buyer guide outline','Content','Help an authorized customer compare scope and coordination before choosing a provider.',[
'Write from the buyer’s decision rather than the provider’s list of selling points.',
'Explain the questions to ask about assessment, service boundaries, documentation, access, and communication.',
'Use a worksheet the reader can complete with any qualified provider; do not force every answer into a sales claim.',
'Keep technical, legal, insurance, health, and regulatory conclusions with the qualified professionals responsible for those decisions.'],[
('Reader','{buyer} managing {segment}','The decision priority is {priority}.'),('Service questions','{objection}','Clarify {intent} before comparing proposals.'),('Evidence request','{proof}','Ask for {segment_proof} where appropriate.'),('Coordination worksheet','{fields}','Document authority, access, scope, and the agreed next action.')],
'A more informed scope conversation and fewer unresolved coordination questions.','A buyer guide should not present a provider’s unverified claims as neutral selection criteria.',SEARCH)
task('service-video-brief','Service video brief','Content','Plan a concise, accessible explanation of the service and the next step.',[
'Choose one buyer question and one action the viewer should understand by the end.',
'Use permissioned, non-graphic visuals and remove unnecessary identifying or sensitive details.',
'Write a transcript and captions that carry the same useful explanation as the video.',
'Publish the video beside relevant text and a clear next step; avoid autoplay that interferes with accessibility or page performance.'],[
('Opening question','{objection}','Name the {service} decision for {segment}.'),('Scene plan','{asset}','Use only approved evidence and explain what the viewer is seeing.'),('Key explanation','{intent}','Keep the explanation directed to the {buyer}.'),('Close','Prepare the next conversation','Ask for {fields}; link to the service scope or contact path.')],
'Viewers who understand the service and reach a relevant next action.','A dramatic video without a clear service explanation can attract attention without helping customers.',SEARCH)
TASKS=[t for t in TASKS if t['slug'] != 'facilities-outreach-brief']
assert len(SERVICES)==10 and len(SEGMENTS)==10 and len(TASKS)==40, (len(SERVICES),len(SEGMENTS),len(TASKS))
